gxr-key-remap is maintained as a native package because the daemons and their
Ubuntu service integration are released from the same repository.

Launchpad versions must be unique. For subsequent PPA uploads, add a changelog
entry and increment the +gxrN component. The changelog targets resolute with a
~26.04.N suffix; publish.sh reuses that entry for every other supported series
with its own ~XX.XX.N suffix.

Publishing is performed in an Ubuntu 26.04 Podman container, so Debian package
tools do not need to be installed on the host. Use ./publish.sh --no-upload for
a signed dry run and ./publish.sh to build, validate, sign, and upload the
source packages. The host needs Podman, Git, and GnuPG.
